# Redirects for the Graphing Calculator site.
# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify `_redirects` format: <from> <to> <status>.
# These cover legacy / typo entry points; the canonical routes are the
# <to> targets. No mass redirects — one rule per genuine alias.

# Canonical domain migration (Firoz, 2026-09-29): the *.pages.dev origin
# should permanently redirect to the production domain. Cloudflare Pages
# `_redirects` matches on path only (verified: a host-specific source rule
# never fires), and the Pages worker only sees /api/* routes, so a
# server-side host redirect is not possible here. The redirect is therefore
# implemented as a tiny inline script in src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro
# (allow-listed by sha256 in public/_headers), which bounces browsers from
# graphing-calc.pages.dev to graphingcalculator.online, preserving path,
# query, and hash. Canonical tags + sitemap already point at the apex
# domain, so search engines consolidate there regardless.

/calculator/ /graphing-calculator/ 301
/graphing-calculator.html /graphing-calculator/ 301
/calculators.html /calculators/ 301
/functions.html /functions/ 301
/examples.html /examples/ 301
/learn.html /learn/ 301
/home/ / 301
/functions/ /math-functions/ 301
/functions/* /math-functions/:splat 301
